{
  "schema_version": "0.1.0",
  "concept": "闭塞确认 (Block Confirmation) — one responsible party per service at a time",
  "canonical_contract": {
    "zh": "proposal.md",
    "en": "proposal.en.md"
  },
  "methodology_source_zh": "方法论移植自铁路调度：同一区间同一时刻只有一列车，交接必须闭塞确认。适老服务同理——同一服务同一时刻只有一个责任主体（AI 或人工），AI 块必须先释放、人工块才占用；无间隙、无重叠。",
  "methodology_source_en": "Methodology transplanted from railway dispatching: one train per block section at a time; handover requires block confirmation. Elderly services likewise — one responsible party (AI or human) per service at a time; the AI block must be released before the human block is occupied; no gap, no overlap.",
  "lens_zh": "透镜：老人的一天——服务链按老人从起床到入睡的完整生活设计（晨间用药提醒→上午就医→午间助餐→下午办事/数字帮扶→晚间安全→睡前回访确认），而非按服务点清单设计。",
  "lens_en": "Lens: An Elder's Day — the service chain is designed around a full day from waking to sleeping (morning medication reminder -> morning clinic visit -> midday meals -> afternoon errands/digital aid -> evening safety -> bedtime follow-up), not around a service-point inventory.",
  "negative_space_baseline_zh": "无AI基线：无任何AI服务时，老人的一天仍能通过社区志愿者、家庭与传统文化服务完整度过。AI 是可关闭的叠加层；闭塞确认确保其关闭时无间隙（老人不会没人管）。",
  "negative_space_baseline_en": "No-AI baseline: without any AI service, an elder's day still works through community volunteers, family and traditional services. AI is a shuttable overlay; block confirmation ensures no gap remains when it is shut (the elder is never left unattended).",
  "scenario_count": 10,
